  "aiContextParagraph": "The investigation into illegal wiretapping activities targeting President Prabowo Subianto has escalated, with the Indonesian National Police (Polri) confirming the reassignment of three high-ranking generals who have been named as suspects. The case, which has drawn significant attention, involves allegations of intelligence gathering aimed at destabilizing the administration. Reports indicate that suspects include figures linked to investigations into treason, with some officials suggesting that intellectual actors may be orchestrating the actions. President Prabowo has previously alluded to the presence of internal sabotage and political intrigue shortly after his inauguration. Legal experts and public officials continue to debate the legal framework surrounding the case, questioning whether charges should fall under the Electronic Information and Transactions (ITE) Law or more severe treason statutes, as authorities work to determine the scope of the alleged conspiracy against the state.",
